<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<catalogue xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/catalogueSchema" id="b174-c09d-3660-b001" name="Battle Brothers (Upgrade Pilot v3.6.0)" revision="8" battleScribeVersion="2.03" library="false" gameSystemId="b174-c09d-3660-f001" gameSystemRevision="2">
  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c100" name="Battleborn" hidden="false"><description>If the majority of this unit has Battleborn, roll at the beginning of a round when Shaken; on 4+, remove Shaken.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c101" name="Fearless" hidden="false"><description>After failing a morale test, this unit has a chance to turn the failure into a pass on a 4+.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c102" name="Hero" hidden="false"><description>May attach to an eligible multi-model unit under the hero attachment rules; its morale can be used for that unit.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c103" name="Tough(X)" hidden="false"><description>Requires X wounds to be removed. Track wounds on individual models and apply the Tough wound-allocation rules.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c104" name="Versatile Expert" hidden="false"><description>When activated, choose one benefit for these models until the end of their activation: +1 AP on attacks, or +1 to hit on attacks.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c105" name="Strider" hidden="false"><description>Ignores difficult terrain penalties while moving.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c106" name="Armor(2+)" hidden="false"><description>This unit has the listed 2+ armour value; use the Armor rules in the current Grimdark Future reference.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c107" name="Scout" hidden="false"><description>Uses a special pre-game deployment/movement option; consult the current core rules for distance and timing.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c108" name="Stealth" hidden="false"><description>Makes this unit harder to hit with shooting when the required range/target conditions apply.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c109" name="Relentless" hidden="false"><description>When firing during a Hold action, unmodified hit rolls of 6 produce an additional hit.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c10a" name="Fast" hidden="false"><description>Increases the distance moved by Advance, Rush and Charge actions.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c10b" name="Ambush" hidden="false"><description>May be held off-table and deployed later under the reserve deployment rules.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c10c" name="Immobile" hidden="false"><description>May only take Hold actions.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c10d" name="Transport(X)" hidden="false"><description>Carries eligible friendly models up to the listed capacity; follow transport embark, disembark and destruction rules.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c10e" name="Fear(X)" hidden="false"><description>Adds X to this unit's effective wounds for determining the winner of melee.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c10f" name="Vanguard" hidden="false"><description>After deployment, may reposition within 9 inches of its starting position, staying over 9 inches from non-Vanguard enemy units.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c110" name="Artillery" hidden="false"><description>Artillery unit restrictions apply; consult the current Grimdark Future core rules.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c111" name="Cumbersome" hidden="false"><description>Restricted to Hold or Advance; cannot fire if it moves.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c112" name="Aircraft" hidden="false"><description>Uses aircraft-specific movement, deployment and targeting restrictions.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c113" name="AP(X)" hidden="false"><description>Targets suffer an X penalty to Defense rolls against this weapon's hits.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c114" name="Blast(X)" hidden="false"><description>Spreads hits across multiple models, up to the number of models in the target unit; check the current Blast procedure.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c115" name="Reliable" hidden="false"><description>Uses improved hit accuracy as defined by the current core rules.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c116" name="Anti-Cover" hidden="false"><description>Counters the target's cover benefits; check the current core rules for precise interaction.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c117" name="Assault" hidden="false"><description>May shoot under the additional movement circumstances allowed by the Assault weapon rule.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c118" name="Surge" hidden="false"><description>Weapon has the Surge special effect; consult the current weapon rule reference.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c119" name="Smash" hidden="false"><description>When attacking beyond half the weapon range, target re-rolls unmodified Defense results of 6.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c11a" name="Takedown" hidden="false"><description>Weapon has the Takedown targeting effect; consult the current weapon rule reference.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c11b" name="Spell Amplifier" hidden="false"><description>Weapon has a spell-related special effect; consult the current Army Forge special rules.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c11c" name="Thrust" hidden="false"><description>Weapon has a charge/movement interaction; consult the current weapon rule reference.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c11d" name="Deadly(X)" hidden="false"><description>Each unsaved hit deals X wounds to a single model, without spilling excess wounds to other models.</description></rule>
    <rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c11e" name="Unstoppable" hidden="false"><description>Ignores Regeneration and negative attack modifiers not caused by the attacking model's own special rules.</description></rule>
  </sharedRules>
